          </size>
         </property>
         <property name="toolTip">
          <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;On by default: after the search, the theoretical fragment masses of the best PrSM of each spectrum that no deconvoluted mass matched are searched in the centroided MS/MS peaks, and the matched masses are added to the spectra (written to &amp;lt;name&amp;gt;_post_ms2.msalign). For a spectrum file &amp;lt;name&amp;gt;_ms2.msalign, toppic reads the peaks from TopFD's SQLite database &amp;lt;name&amp;gt;.sqlite (run TopFD without -N, --no-sql) through its own copy &amp;lt;name&amp;gt;_toppic.sqlite. Clear it to skip this step; TopFD's database is then not needed. (when cleared: toppic -D, --disable-post-match)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Post mass matching (needs the TopFD SQLite database)</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
